      "message": "Version numbered flags should not be used for default-enabled features in general; I think we should remove this overload of isFeatureEnabled that allows passing true. This is because the rollback scheme (feature becomes disabled if the module version rolls back to a version lower than the flag value) does not make sense if the flag is default enabled.\n\nInstead, you could have a method like `DeviceConfigUtils.isTetheringFeatureForceDisabled(CONFIG_DISABLE_CLAT_ADDRESS_TRANSLATE)`, which just checks if the flag value is !\u003d 0 (not a version number)",
